__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/

# uv.lock is deliberately NOT tracked. Nothing consumes it: CI installs with
# `pip install -e ".[mcp,http]"` and the sdist resolves from pyproject.toml, so the
# lock's only real effect was pinning contributors who follow CONTRIBUTING.md's
# `uv sync` onto a stale resolution — which is how a fixed-upstream CVE stayed
# installable here long after the fix shipped. pyproject.toml is the single source
# of truth for the dependency surface.
# This entry is load-bearing, not cosmetic: `uv sync` regenerates the lock, and this
# tree is swept by a nightly `git add -A`, so without the ignore the file returns on
# its own within a day and the decision silently reverts.
uv.lock
